"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3984980499/worktree/.pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json","content":"        {\n          \"name\": \"common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n          \"program\": \"go\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"test\",\n            \"-race\",\n            \"./internal/pose\",\n            \"./internal/cli\",\n            \"./internal/mcpserver\",\n            \"-run\",\n            \"InProcessRun|CloseoutHandoff|AHandoff|NoHandoff|PendingJudgment|InProcessWrapper|EveryMCPRoute|OnlyAdmitted|ReadOnlyWrappers|KeepTheProcessBoundary|TypedHandoff|StableAndADone|TheMCPPlanIsTheDomainPlan|AdmittedWritesAreExactly|Golden|BlockedOrUnstable|TheDigestOfAHandoff|ACancelledCaller|ACompletionThat|AbandonedRuns|NotTakenWhenTheSpawn|APanicInAnInProcess|APendingMechanicalStep|TheHandoffKeepsTheSelectedProject|TheHandoffOverMCP\",\n            \"-count=1\"\n          ],\n          \"severity\": \"required\",\n          \"evidenceClass\": \"integration\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n          \"program\": \"go\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"test\",\n            \"./internal/pose\",\n            \"./internal/mcpserver\",\n            \"-run\",\n            \"PageByGeneration|ACursor|HostileCursor|ExpiredCursor|APositionOutside|AContinuation|AnIssuedCursor|EveryPage|PageLimitIsBounded|EquivalentFilters|APageStates|APageCarries|PageCost|DoesNotReverify|SymlinkTarget|PreservesSizeAndModTime|NullCursor|FiltersThatSerialize|ACursorAlias|OmittedSort|AnAlias|AnExplicit|Pagination|ListToolsShareThePaginationSchema\",","numLines":25,"startLine":2642,"totalLines":2693}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Js67hp3ysG8utqNALQC3yW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrurcxfeSu76XgL4zHzi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CYqdo6gx9MUZEbSHcRdbQy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3984980499/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","offset":176,"limit":62},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":90673,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1116},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"85e4e2c9-8b32-4237-a115-b6d7dcc26b19","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:52:10.101Z","request_id":"req_011CgrurcinLs646awNbEN8C","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CYqdo6gx9MUZEbSHcRdbQy":{"file_path":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3984980499/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","offset":176,"limit":62}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CYqdo6gx9MUZEbSHcRdbQy","type":"tool_result","content":"176\tmutable graph.\n177\t\n178\t## Amendment: common operations and the typed handoff (B31)\n179\t\n180\tSpec `pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff` fixes how an MCP route shares code\n181\twith the CLI, without a resident service:\n182\t\n183\t- **Five route classes.** Every MCP tool is declared one of: domain-direct,\n184\t  cli-wrapper, read-only-planning, admitted-write, external-handoff. A test keeps\n185\t  the declaration equal to the advertised catalog, so a tool cannot ship without a\n186\t  class, and checks that the tools classed admitted-write are exactly the four\n187\t  governance write points (`pose_action_open`, `pose_action_resolve`,\n188\t  `pose_action_fulfil`, `pose_review_attest`), which revalidate authority, assurance,\n189\t  policy and subjects themselves. Other tools that start an agent or record a run\n190\t  (`pose_delegate_*`) or request a gate (`pose_validate_*`) carry their own catalog\n191\t  risk classes and are not admitted writes of the governance state. The MCP-Conductor-Harness boundary (`pose_validate_*`,\n192\t  `conductor_run_*`) is external-handoff: `tools/call` never becomes the execution\n193\t  of a project's checks.\n194\t- **No second binary for read-only operations the CLI package owns.** The domain\n195\t  wrappers run a registered command function in process when it is read-only and\n196\t  bounded (`suggest`, `followups`), and only when that answers as the spawn of the\n197\t  installed binary would: not when `POSE_EXECUTABLE` names another binary, and not\n198\t  when the file the server started from has been replaced since (`pose update` writes\n199\t  the new engine at the same path), because a spawned run then uses the updated engine\n200\t  and the server still holds the old one in memory (spec\n201\t  `pose-mcp-server-survives-self-update` R2). In those cases the wrapper spawns as it\n202\t  always did. The function is the single source: results,\n203\t  errors and coverage are the CLI's. The contract of the spawned run is kept: a\n204\t  non-zero exit is an error carrying the command's message, and a deadline or a\n205\t  cancellation is an execution failure with no verdict (the run cannot be killed, so\n206\t  it finishes in the background and writes nothing; a caller that has already\n207\t  cancelled never starts it, a completion that races a cancellation is discarded, and\n208\t  the runs alive at once, abandoned ones included, are capped so that repeated\n209\t  timeouts cannot accumulate work). The gates keep the process\n210\t  boundary: they are long, can be killed on a deadline, and must not leave a half\n211\t  verdict. Spawn attempts and in-process runs are counted so the extraction is\n212\t  evidenced by count, not by promise.\n213\t- **A typed handoff, not an execution.** A closeout plan with steps left carries an\n214\t  `OperationHandoff`: the operation and scope, the CLI invocation as structured\n215\t  arguments (no shell line), the plan, spec, revision, policy and generation digests\n216\t  it was computed from, the authority it needs, the arguments the performer still owes and the handoff does\n217\t  not carry (the `--reviewer` execution identity when a mechanical attestation is\n218\t  pending), how the outcome comes back and when it stops being valid, and\n219\t  `executes: false`. The request id is derived from the\n220\t  operation, scope and plan digest, so a stale handoff is not mistaken for the\n221\t  current one. It names the project the caller selected, by its logical id and the\n222\t  digest of its root and never by a path (the MCP contract exposes no filesystem\n223\t  root), and does not retarget itself. It carries no secret, grants no authority and infers no context:\n224\t  `pose close --apply` takes no context flag, its binding is the full plan digest it\n225\t  names (the digest the apply compares, with its `sha256:` prefix), and the performer\n226\t  verifies the authority and revision with a fresh `pose context` in the target root\n227\t  before applying. A plan that is terminal, has any blocked step or blocker, or whose\n228\t  read view is unknown has none.\n229\t- **Not shared by sharing code.** stdio is not an IPC channel shared between\n230\t  clients; an MCP transport gains no Execution Identity, signature or human presence\n231\t  of the CLI by calling the same function.\n232\t\n233\t## Related specs\n234\t\n235\t- [B31](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md)\n236\t- [B33](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md)\n237\t- [B35](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"c7c33ac6-68e6-4f83-a4f8-f8b253e83292","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:52:10.106Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3984980499/worktree/.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md","content":"mutable graph.\n\n## Amendment: common operations and the typed handoff (B31)\n\nSpec `pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff` fixes how an MCP route shares code\nwith the CLI, without a resident service:\n\n- **Five route classes.** Every MCP tool is declared one of: domain-direct,\n  cli-wrapper, read-only-planning, admitted-write, external-handoff. A test keeps\n  the declaration equal to the advertised catalog, so a tool cannot ship without a\n  class, and checks that the tools classed admitted-write are exactly the four\n  governance write points (`pose_action_open`, `pose_action_resolve`,\n  `pose_action_fulfil`, `pose_review_attest`), which revalidate authority, assurance,\n  policy and subjects themselves. Other tools that start an agent or record a run\n  (`pose_delegate_*`) or request a gate (`pose_validate_*`) carry their own catalog\n  risk classes and are not admitted writes of the governance state. The MCP-Conductor-Harness boundary (`pose_validate_*`,\n  `conductor_run_*`) is external-handoff: `tools/call` never becomes the execution\n  of a project's checks.\n- **No second binary for read-only operations the CLI package owns.** The domain\n  wrappers run a registered command function in process when it is read-only and\n  bounded (`suggest`, `followups`), and only when that answers as the spawn of the\n  installed binary would: not when `POSE_EXECUTABLE` names another binary, and not\n  when the file the server started from has been replaced since (`pose update` writes\n  the new engine at the same path), because a spawned run then uses the updated engine\n  and the server still holds the old one in memory (spec\n  `pose-mcp-server-survives-self-update` R2). In those cases the wrapper spawns as it\n  always did. The function is the single source: results,\n  errors and coverage are the CLI's. The contract of the spawned run is kept: a\n  non-zero exit is an error carrying the command's message, and a deadline or a\n  cancellation is an execution failure with no verdict (the run cannot be killed, so\n  it finishes in the background and writes nothing; a caller that has already\n  cancelled never starts it, a completion that races a cancellation is discarded, and\n  the runs alive at once, abandoned ones included, are capped so that repeated\n  timeouts cannot accumulate work). The gates keep the process\n  boundary: they are long, can be killed on a deadline, and must not leave a half\n  verdict. Spawn attempts and in-process runs are counted so the extraction is\n  evidenced by count, not by promise.\n- **A typed handoff, not an execution.** A closeout plan with steps left carries an\n  `OperationHandoff`: the operation and scope, the CLI invocation as structured\n  arguments (no shell line), the plan, spec, revision, policy and generation digests\n  it was computed from, the authority it needs, the arguments the performer still owes and the handoff does\n  not carry (the `--reviewer` execution identity when a mechanical attestation is\n  pending), how the outcome comes back and when it stops being valid, and\n  `executes: false`. The request id is derived from the\n  operation, scope and plan digest, so a stale handoff is not mistaken for the\n  current one. It names the project the caller selected, by its logical id and the\n  digest of its root and never by a path (the MCP contract exposes no filesystem\n  root), and does not retarget itself. It carries no secret, grants no authority and infers no context:\n  `pose close --apply` takes no context flag, its binding is the full plan digest it\n  names (the digest the apply compares, with its `sha256:` prefix), and the performer\n  verifies the authority and revision with a fresh `pose context` in the target root\n  before applying. A plan that is terminal, has any blocked step or blocker, or whose\n  read view is unknown has none.\n- **Not shared by sharing code.** stdio is not an IPC channel shared between\n  clients; an MCP transport gains no Execution Identity, signature or human presence\n  of the CLI by calling the same function.\n\n## Related specs\n\n- [B31](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff.md)\n- [B33](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches.md)\n- [B35](../specs/2026-10-14-pose-optional-worktree-runtime.md)","numLines":62,"startLine":176,"totalLines":238}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CYqdo6gx9MUZEbSHcRdbQy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
