{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrutqpNvj8gaGGa8SVwE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approve this change. It meets the spec, and I found no blocker. There are two low follow-ups, each written as an accepted risk. POSE may still refuse the draft because of two required tools; see the tools section below.\n\n**What I ran**\n- The spec's tests with the race detector, across `internal/pose`, `internal/cli` and `internal/mcpserver`: all passed.\n- `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict`: passed. Its only output was repository-wide orphan warnings that predate this change.\n- `pose surface-check --spec … --strict`: passed, with 0 findings over 195 results.\n- `pose review-check spec:…` and `pose closeout-check spec:…`: both exit non-zero. They report that the review is still pending and the lifecycle is not done. That is the state this review exists to resolve, so they can't pass until the conclusion is recorded. I marked them `deferred`, not `passed`. The rules require a required tool to be `passed`, so POSE may refuse the draft on this alone.\n- `pose validate`, `pose assess …` and `pose suggest review` were refused by my permission profile. For the two validate tools I cite the sealed validation evidence (`build:pose-mcp/go/build`, `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`) and say in the rationale that I didn't rerun them. The recommended tools are `not-used`.\n\n**What I checked**\n- **In-process runs:** `runInProcess` (`pose-mcp/internal/pose/common_operation.go:114-179`) handles each case correctly:\n  - a caller that is already cancelled, or cancelled while waiting for a slot, never starts the command;\n  - a completion that races a cancellation is discarded;\n  - abandoned runs keep their slot (four in total);\n  - a panic becomes a failed run;\n  - a non-zero exit becomes an error carrying the command's message.\n- **Self-update guard:** `pose update` replaces the binary by renaming a new file over it (`internal/cli/maintenance.go:531`). So the `os.SameFile` check sees a new file after an update, and the in-process route is skipped. `POSE_EXECUTABLE` is also checked first.\n- **Spawn parity:** the spawned run sets `POSE_USAGE_SUPPRESS_CLI=1` (`internal/pose/cli.go:160`), so running in process loses no usage records.\n- **Handoff matches the CLI:** its arguments (`pose close <scope> --apply --digest <digest>`, plus a `--reviewer` the performer must supply) match what `cmdClosePlan` accepts (`internal/cli/closeout_plan.go:30-66`). The digest is compared as the full string (`closeout_plan.go:317`).\n- **No paths in the response (round-8 sweep):** none of the handoff's fields carries a path; the project is named by id and root digest. `execution_plan` is the existing `CloseoutPlan`, and the MCP route never fills its `checkpoint`.\n- **Docs:** `POSE.md` and its scaffold copies document the handoff and route classes the same way the code behaves.\n\n**Defects**\n- **F2, low, follow-up** (`pose-mcp/internal/pose/common_operation.go:153`): an in-process run gets `Store.Root` as it is. A spawned run instead lets the CLI work out the project root from that directory, so a root that is a subdirectory of a project would resolve differently. The server only selects project roots, so no known path differs today. The spec already discloses this.\n- **F3, low, follow-up, new** (`pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/delegate_tools.go:54`, counter at `common_operation.go:54-56`): the five `pose_delegate_*` routes start the POSE binary through `defaultDelegateRunner`, which doesn't add to `CLISpawnAttempts`. That counter is documented as counting every attempt \"to start the POSE binary\", so it undercounts.\n\n**Structural facts** (all three mapped under `design-causality`):\n- SD-060e7b67, the ADR amendment, maps to R8 and D1.\n- SD-8d3051b9 and SD-ac7fe101, the validation-matrix changes, map to R9 and R1. They are the `common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration` check and the run-pattern fix in `99b18c04`.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F2\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/common_operation.go\",\n      \"line\": 153,\n      \"summary\": \"An in-process run hands the command Store.Root as it is, while a spawned run starts in that directory and lets the CLI resolve the project root; a root that is a subdirectory of a project would resolve differently. No known path differs because the server selects project roots; declared in the spec's Known gaps.\",\n      \"action\": \"Resolve the root as the CLI dispatcher does before an in-process run, or reject a root that is not a project root.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F3\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/delegate_tools.go\",\n      \"line\": 54,\n      \"summary\": \"The pose_delegate_* cli-wrapper routes start the POSE binary through defaultDelegateRunner without incrementing CLISpawnAttempts, which common_operation.go:54-56 documents as counting every attempt of a wrapper to start the POSE binary; the spawn measurement R9 asks for undercounts those routes.\",\n      \"action\": \"Count the delegate runner's spawns in CLISpawnAttempts (or a per-route counter), or narrow the counter's documentation to the runCLI/runCLIExit wrappers.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the assumptions in the spec's Known gaps and Residual risks against the code. Verified facts: pose update replaces the binary by rename (maintenance.go:531), so the os.SameFile check detects it; the spawn suppresses CLI usage (cli.go:160), so in-process runs lose no telemetry; the apply compares the full digest (closeout_plan.go:317). Unresolved but accepted as risks: the root-resolution difference (F2), the unbounded per-run work of followups and the hand-declared route classes, all disclosed with follow-ups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"runInProcess checks cancellation before admission, after admission and after completion. Slots are released by the goroutine itself, panics included. Reran the suite with go test -race: it passed, including the concurrency and abandoned-slot tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The handoff is an additive omitempty field on the pose_closeout_state include_plan response; the existing execution_plan is unchanged. The catalog golden only gains description text. The in-process wrappers keep runCLI's error contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A non-zero exit returns 'pose <cmd> failed: <message>'. A deadline, a cancellation or a full slot set returns GateExecutionError with a cause and a cleanup note, never a verdict. A panic becomes a failed run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The CLI registers suggest and followups in an init linked into the pose binary that serves MCP. The parity test compares the spawned built binary with the in-process wrapper. The handoff's argv was run against the CLI apply.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the response shape, the catalog golden and the self-update path. The response change is additive. The in-process route is skipped when POSE_EXECUTABLE is set or the installed binary has been replaced, which keeps pose-mcp-server-survives-self-update R2. F2 is the only known divergence and cannot be reached by a root the server selects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reran the spec's tests with -race across the three packages, all passing. Checked CloseoutHandoff against cmdClosePlan's flags and the apply's digest comparison. Blocked, terminal and unknown-view plans get no handoff.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-dc3138c2fd99035e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the design against D1 and R1-R9. Running suggest and followups in process from the CLI's own registered command functions gives one source of results without a second implementation (R1, R8). The typed handoff, derived only from PlanCloseout's output, gives MCP a read-only closeout route that applies nothing (R3-R5). The route inventory, held equal to the catalog and to the governance-write risk class by tests, keeps writes at the four domain write points (R6, R7).\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-060e7b67\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR amendment records the route classes, the in-process admission rule and the typed handoff that D1 adopts, and that R8 requires to be recorded before the code.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-8d3051b9\",\n          \"basis\": \"R9\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Adds the required common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration check that qualifies R1-R9 under -race.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-ac7fe101\",\n          \"basis\": \"R1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Adjusts the check's run pattern (commit 99b18c04 drops the renamed handoff-target test) so the matrix runs the tests in the requirement trace.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Read the handoff paragraph in POSE.md:844 and in the scaffold dist/POSE.md:831: they are identical, and the pt-BR copies cover the same content. The text matches CloseoutHandoff's fields and conditions and the in-process admission rule. The ADR amendment matches the code.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"milestone-exit-gate-pose-shared-runtime-common-domain-handoff\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"B31 keeps results, errors and authority from one source: the CLI command function. The extracted wrappers count zero spawns. P04: the handoff states that apply takes no context flag and that the performer verifies context in the target root, which is an explicit limitation. MCP offers a read-only plan plus a typed handoff, and P15 parity is tested. Writes stay at the four admitted points. The gates and the delegate harness keep the process boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Execution failures say whether the command started, ran in the background or was discarded, and that nothing was written. The handoff states required_inputs, its receipt path and its invalidation. Remediation is actionable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Every trace test of R1-R9 matches the check's -run pattern, and the suite passed when I reran it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the change set's files with the spec's Artifacts list: they match. No closeout-applying MCP tool, scheduler or retry was added. Moving the semantics into the domain package is left as a declared follow-up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Swept the fields of the changed MCP response: the handoff carries no filesystem path, secret or reviewer identity. Its argv is structured and executes nothing. The authority line is a hint and grants nothing. Only read-only commands are registered to run in process.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The smallest sufficient alternative, a registry of two existing command functions plus a derived handoff struct, was the one chosen; no new runtime or tool was added. The choice is invalidated if a registered command writes, or if followups' work becomes unbounded in practice; both are disclosed with follow-ups.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exit 0. The output holds only repository-wide orphan warnings that predate this change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused the command. The sealed structure:design-dc3138c2fd99035e evidence is cited under design-causality.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused pose assess.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused pose assess.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused pose assess.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Run; exits non-zero with 'lifecycle status is not done' and next action 'record or remediate a fresh review'. The check can only pass after this review is recorded and the spec is closed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Run; exits non-zero because review.approved=false: the review it checks is this one. It can only pass after this conclusion is recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused the command.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff --strict myself: exit 0, 1 target, 195 results, 0 findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Not rerun by me: my permission profile refused pose validate. The sealed strict validation passed. I reran the spec's suite with go test -race, which passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Not rerun by me: my permission profile refused pose validate. The sealed strict module validation passed. I reran the spec's suite with go test -race, which passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1070,"cache_read_input_tokens":100733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1070},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"f5a17207-7c0d-42e4-af11-b487a2797d5f","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:53:49.387Z","request_id":"req_011CgrutqbjkHu4wb9EJQF8i"}
{"duration_api_ms":251609,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"[private-session]","total_cost_usd":1.9279908000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":96,"cache_creation_input_tokens":97238,"cache_read_input_tokens":3125214,"output_tokens":26233,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":9769},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":97238,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8467,"cache_read_input_tokens":100733,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1070},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":96,"outputTokens":26233,"cacheReadInputTokens":3125214,"cacheCreationInputTokens":97238,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.9279908000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":9769,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":97238,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qm9Fke42ckeb8JpFUbvHQv","tool_input":{"command":"which pose; go version; go build -o /tmp/pose-review-bin-3984980499/pose ./cmd/pose && echo built","timeout":300000,"description":"Locate pose and build it from the reviewed head"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01JhBZoMxCecrBdcPA6e6zCE","tool_input":{"command":"which pose && pose version","description":"Locate the installed pose binary"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01J8R27QYLujhEa4awxEpBUZ","tool_input":{"command":"cd /var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3984980499/worktree && command -v pose; ls pose-mcp/bin 2>/dev/null","description":"Check for an installed or prebuilt pose binary"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_019WS3LiFMscVhNcA8t33qCZ","tool_input":{"command":"pose artifact-check --spec pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff --strict >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"artifact-check exit=$?\"; pose surface-check --spec pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff --strict 2>&1 | tail -6; echo \"surface exit=${pipestatus[1]}\"","timeout":300000,"description":"Get exit codes of artifact-check and surface-check"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TUaGu2ruGN138ssmjmfxqg","tool_input":{"command":"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp 2>&1 | tail -25","timeout":600000,"description":"Run strict validation of the pose-mcp module","run_in_background":true}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01V9NceejHbHfgy2usTq1tZa","tool_input":{"command":"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp 2>&1 | tail -25","timeout":600000,"description":"Run strict validation of the pose-mcp module"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xy9mJRjXsezgytLTL2CG9Y","tool_input":{"command":"pose assess design --spec pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff --json 2>&1 | head -c 4000","timeout":300000,"description":"Run the recommended design assessment"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_017TvC1Rrwx5rvyW7zSup8UE","tool_input":{"command":"pose suggest review --path pose-mcp 2>&1 | head -40","timeout":120000,"description":"Run the recommended review suggestion for pose-mcp"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_015rLctdQXdeRUM4ohVRfBjo","tool_input":{"command":"cd /var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3984980499/worktree && git diff 7e40761d..d9cd4417 -- POSE.md | grep -n \"^[+-]\" | grep -i -n \"handoff\\|route class\\|domain-direct\\|cli-wrapper\" | head -20; diff POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md && echo SAME-EN; diff locales/pt-BR/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md && echo SAME-PT","description":"Check manual handoff documentation and scaffold parity"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":60,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I approve this change. It meets the spec, and I found no blocker. There are two low follow-ups, each written as an accepted risk. POSE may still refuse the draft because of two required tools; see the tools section below.\n\n**What I ran**\n- The spec's tests with the race detector, across `internal/pose`, `internal/cli` and `internal/mcpserver`: all passed.\n- `pose artifact-check --spec … --strict`: passed. Its only output was repository-wide orphan warnings that predate this change.\n- `pose surface-check --spec … --strict`: passed, with 0 findings over 195 results.\n- `pose review-check spec:…` and `pose closeout-check spec:…`: both exit non-zero. They report that the review is still pending and the lifecycle is not done. That is the state this review exists to resolve, so they can't pass until the conclusion is recorded. I marked them `deferred`, not `passed`. The rules require a required tool to be `passed`, so POSE may refuse the draft on this alone.\n- `pose validate`, `pose assess …` and `pose suggest review` were refused by my permission profile. For the two validate tools I cite the sealed validation evidence (`build:pose-mcp/go/build`, `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`) and say in the rationale that I didn't rerun them. The recommended tools are `not-used`.\n\n**What I checked**\n- **In-process runs:** `runInProcess` (`pose-mcp/internal/pose/common_operation.go:114-179`) handles each case correctly:\n  - a caller that is already cancelled, or cancelled while waiting for a slot, never starts the command;\n  - a completion that races a cancellation is discarded;\n  - abandoned runs keep their slot (four in total);\n  - a panic becomes a failed run;\n  - a non-zero exit becomes an error carrying the command's message.\n- **Self-update guard:** `pose update` replaces the binary by renaming a new file over it (`internal/cli/maintenance.go:531`). So the `os.SameFile` check sees a new file after an update, and the in-process route is skipped. `POSE_EXECUTABLE` is also checked first.\n- **Spawn parity:** the spawned run sets `POSE_USAGE_SUPPRESS_CLI=1` (`internal/pose/cli.go:160`), so running in process loses no usage records.\n- **Handoff matches the CLI:** its arguments (`pose close <scope> --apply --digest <digest>`, plus a `--reviewer` the performer must supply) match what `cmdClosePlan` accepts (`internal/cli/closeout_plan.go:30-66`). The digest is compared as the full string (`closeout_plan.go:317`).\n- **No paths in the response (round-8 sweep):** none of the handoff's fields carries a path; the project is named by id and root digest. `execution_plan` is the existing `CloseoutPlan`, and the MCP route never fills its `checkpoint`.\n- **Docs:** `POSE.md` and its scaffold copies document the handoff and route classes the same way the code behaves.\n\n**Defects**\n- **F2, low, follow-up** (`pose-mcp/internal/pose/common_operation.go:153`): an in-process run gets `Store.Root` as it is. A spawned run instead lets the CLI work out the project root from that directory, so a root that is a subdirectory of a project would resolve differently. The server only selects project roots, so no known path differs today. The spec already discloses this.\n- **F3, low, follow-up, new** (`pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/delegate_tools.go:54`, counter at `common_operation.go:54-56`): the five `pose_delegate_*` routes start the POSE binary through `defaultDelegateRunner`, which doesn't add to `CLISpawnAttempts`. That counter is documented as counting every attempt \"to start the POSE binary\", so it undercounts.\n\n**Structural facts** (all three mapped under `design-causality`):\n- SD-060e7b67, the ADR amendment, maps to R8 and D1.\n- SD-8d3051b9 and SD-ac7fe101, the validation-matrix changes, map to R9 and R1. They are the `common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration` check and the run-pattern fix in `99b18c04`.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F2\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/common_operation.go\",\n      \"line\": 153,\n      \"summary\": \"An in-process run hands the command Store.Root as it is, while a spawned run starts in that directory and lets the CLI resolve the project root; a root that is a subdirectory of a project would resolve differently. No known path differs because the server selects project roots; declared in the spec's Known gaps.\",\n      \"action\": \"Resolve the root as the CLI dispatcher does before an in-process run, or reject a root that is not a project root.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F3\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/mcpserver/delegate_tools.go\",\n      \"line\": 54,\n      \"summary\": \"The pose_delegate_* cli-wrapper routes start the POSE binary through defaultDelegateRunner without incrementing CLISpawnAttempts, which common_operation.go:54-56 documents as counting every attempt of a wrapper to start the POSE binary; the spawn measurement R9 asks for undercounts those routes.\",\n      \"action\": \"Count the delegate runner's spawns in CLISpawnAttempts (or a per-route counter), or narrow the counter's documentation to the runCLI/runCLIExit wrappers.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2027-01-08\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the assumptions in the spec's Known gaps and Residual risks against the code. Verified facts: pose update replaces the binary by rename (maintenance.go:531), so the os.SameFile check detects it; the spawn suppresses CLI usage (cli.go:160), so in-process runs lose no telemetry; the apply compares the full digest (closeout_plan.go:317). Unresolved but accepted as risks: the root-resolution difference (F2), the unbounded per-run work of followups and the hand-declared route classes, all disclosed with follow-ups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"runInProcess checks cancellation before admission, after admission and after completion. Slots are released by the goroutine itself, panics included. Reran the suite with go test -race: it passed, including the concurrency and abandoned-slot tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The handoff is an additive omitempty field on the pose_closeout_state include_plan response; the existing execution_plan is unchanged. The catalog golden only gains description text. The in-process wrappers keep runCLI's error contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A non-zero exit returns 'pose <cmd> failed: <message>'. A deadline, a cancellation or a full slot set returns GateExecutionError with a cause and a cleanup note, never a verdict. A panic becomes a failed run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The CLI registers suggest and followups in an init linked into the pose binary that serves MCP. The parity test compares the spawned built binary with the in-process wrapper. The handoff's argv was run against the CLI apply.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"F3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the response shape, the catalog golden and the self-update path. The response change is additive. The in-process route is skipped when POSE_EXECUTABLE is set or the installed binary has been replaced, which keeps pose-mcp-server-survives-self-update R2. F2 is the only known divergence and cannot be reached by a root the server selects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reran the spec's tests with -race across the three packages, all passing. Checked CloseoutHandoff against cmdClosePlan's flags and the apply's digest comparison. Blocked, terminal and unknown-view plans get no handoff.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-dc3138c2fd99035e\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined the design against D1 and R1-R9. Running suggest and followups in process from the CLI's own registered command functions gives one source of results without a second implementation (R1, R8). The typed handoff, derived only from PlanCloseout's output, gives MCP a read-only closeout route that applies nothing (R3-R5). The route inventory, held equal to the catalog and to the governance-write risk class by tests, keeps writes at the four domain write points (R6, R7).\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-060e7b67\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR amendment records the route classes, the in-process admission rule and the typed handoff that D1 adopts, and that R8 requires to be recorded before the code.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-8d3051b9\",\n          \"basis\": \"R9\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Adds the required common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration check that qualifies R1-R9 under -race.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-ac7fe101\",\n          \"basis\": \"R1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"Adjusts the check's run pattern (commit 99b18c04 drops the renamed handoff-target test) so the matrix runs the tests in the requirement trace.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Read the handoff paragraph in POSE.md:844 and in the scaffold dist/POSE.md:831: they are identical, and the pt-BR copies cover the same content. The text matches CloseoutHandoff's fields and conditions and the in-process admission rule. The ADR amendment matches the code.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"milestone-exit-gate-pose-shared-runtime-common-domain-handoff\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"B31 keeps results, errors and authority from one source: the CLI command function. The extracted wrappers count zero spawns. P04: the handoff states that apply takes no context flag and that the performer verifies context in the target root, which is an explicit limitation. MCP offers a read-only plan plus a typed handoff, and P15 parity is tested. Writes stay at the four admitted points. The gates and the delegate harness keep the process boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Execution failures say whether the command started, ran in the background or was discarded, and that nothing was written. The handoff states required_inputs, its receipt path and its invalidation. Remediation is actionable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Every trace test of R1-R9 matches the check's -run pattern, and the suite passed when I reran it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the change set's files with the spec's Artifacts list: they match. No closeout-applying MCP tool, scheduler or retry was added. Moving the semantics into the domain package is left as a declared follow-up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Swept the fields of the changed MCP response: the handoff carries no filesystem path, secret or reviewer identity. Its argv is structured and executes nothing. The authority line is a hint and grants nothing. Only read-only commands are registered to run in process.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The smallest sufficient alternative, a registry of two existing command functions plus a derived handoff struct, was the one chosen; no new runtime or tool was added. The choice is invalidated if a registered command writes, or if followups' work becomes unbounded in practice; both are disclosed with follow-ups.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exit 0. The output holds only repository-wide orphan warnings that predate this change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused the command. The sealed structure:design-dc3138c2fd99035e evidence is cited under design-causality.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused pose assess.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused pose assess.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused pose assess.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Run; exits non-zero with 'lifecycle status is not done' and next action 'record or remediate a fresh review'. The check can only pass after this review is recorded and the spec is closed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Run; exits non-zero because review.approved=false: the review it checks is this one. It can only pass after this conclusion is recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"My permission profile refused the command.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose surface-check --spec pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff --strict myself: exit 0, 1 target, 195 results, 0 findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Not rerun by me: my permission profile refused pose validate. The sealed strict validation passed. I reran the spec's suite with go test -race, which passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Not rerun by me: my permission profile refused pose validate. The sealed strict module validation passed. I reran the spec's suite with go test -race, which passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1151,"type":"result","duration_ms":1056502,"uuid":"b8c74cad-0cf4-4730-affd-23b08906ffc1","ttft_stream_ms":818,"time_to_request_ms":45,"first_content_frame_ms":818,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":96,"outputTokens":26233,"cacheReadInputTokens":3125214,"cacheCreationInputTokens":97238,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.9279908000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":9769,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":97238,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"f